---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Disclosure from '../components/Disclosure.astro';
import { org } from '../data/schema';
import { SITE_URL, SITE_NAME, FACTS_AS_OF } from '../data/site.mjs';

const title = 'Dogear: Kindle Paperwhite and Kindle Case Buying Guides';
const description = 'Independent, plain-English Kindle buying guides: which Paperwhite to buy, cases that fit by model year, plus chargers, stands and page turners. Specs checked against Amazon, clear sourcing.';
const ld = [
  { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@graph': [
    org,
    { '@type': 'WebSite', '@id': new URL('/#website', SITE_URL).toString(), url: SITE_URL + '/', name: SITE_NAME, inLanguage: 'en-US', publisher: { '@id': org['@id'] } },
  ] },
];
---
<Base title={title} description={description} path="/" jsonld={ld}>
  <h1>Kindle buying guides that show their sources</h1>
  <p class="lede">{SITE_NAME} helps you pick a Kindle Paperwhite and the right case for it, without the guesswork. We check specs and prices against Amazon's own pages, tell you what we could not verify, and keep the advice practical.</p>
  <Disclosure />

  <div class="box">
    <h2 id="accessories">Shopping for accessories?</h2>
    <p>Our <a href="/kindle-accessories/"><strong>Kindle accessories guide</strong></a> groups cases, covers, sleeves, stands, chargers and page turners by what they do, shows which ones fit each Kindle model, and lists what you can skip. <a class="btn" href="/kindle-accessories/">See all Kindle accessories</a></p>
  </div>

  <div class="cards">
    <article class="card">
      <span class="pill new">Updated {FACTS_AS_OF}</span>
      <h2><a href="/kindle-paperwhite/">Kindle Paperwhite: which one to buy</a></h2>
      <p>The new 2026 Paperwhite versus the 2024 and 2021 models, Signature Edition versus standard, ads, storage, and who should wait.</p>
      <a class="btn" href="/kindle-paperwhite/">Read the Paperwhite guide</a>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <span class="pill new">New</span>
      <h2><a href="/kindle-paperwhite-case/">Kindle Paperwhite case: fit by model year</a></h2>
      <p>Which case fits the 2026, 2024, 2021 and older Paperwhite, what is still unconfirmed for the new model, and which styles suit how you read.</p>
      <a class="btn" href="/kindle-paperwhite-case/">Read the Paperwhite case guide</a>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <span class="pill new">New</span>
      <h2><a href="/kindle-scribe-case/">Kindle Scribe case: fit and pen storage</a></h2>
      <p>Which case fits the 2022, 2024 and 2025 (11-inch) Scribe and Scribe Colorsoft, how the pen attaches, and what to check about folios and magnets.</p>
      <a class="btn" href="/kindle-scribe-case/">Read the Scribe case guide</a>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <span class="pill new">New</span>
      <h2><a href="/kindle-cover/">Kindle Paperwhite cover: fit, types and 2026 models</a></h2>
      <p>What to check for a Paperwhite cover, 2026 vs 2024 fit, folio vs shell, and when a sleeve is enough instead.</p>
      <a class="btn" href="/kindle-cover/">Read the cover guide</a>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <span class="pill new">New</span>
      <h2><a href="/kindle-sleeve/">Kindle sleeve: sizes, materials and when a sleeve is enough</a></h2>
      <p>Interior sizes against 2026 and 2024 Paperwhite and other Kindles, sleeve vs folio cover, and listing red flags.</p>
      <a class="btn" href="/kindle-sleeve/">Read the sleeve guide</a>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <span class="pill new">New</span>
      <h2><a href="/kindle-stand/">Kindle stand guide: desk, bed and dock</a></h2>
      <p>Desk, gooseneck, pillow and charging stands compared, with what to check about stability, angle and case compatibility.</p>
      <a class="btn" href="/kindle-stand/">Read the stand guide</a>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <span class="pill new">New</span>
      <h2><a href="/kindle-colorsoft-case/">Kindle Colorsoft case: 2024, 2025 and 2026 fit</a></h2>
      <p>Which case fits the 2024 Signature Edition, the 2025 16 GB model and the new 2026 Colorsoft, plus Double Tap, wireless charging and pogo-pin notes.</p>
      <a class="btn" href="/kindle-colorsoft-case/">Read the Colorsoft case guide</a>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <span class="pill new">New</span>
      <h2><a href="/kindle-charger/">Kindle charger guide: ports and adapters</a></h2>
      <p>USB-C or micro-USB by model year, what Amazon says about 5W, 9W and 20W adapters, wireless docks, and what to try when a Kindle will not charge.</p>
      <a class="btn" href="/kindle-charger/">Read the charger guide</a>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <span class="pill new">New</span>
      <h2><a href="/kindle-page-turner/">Kindle page turners: what works</a></h2>
      <p>Amazon's Kindle Click and Page-Turn Cover, clip-on tappers, Double Tap and Kindle app options, with which Kindles support each.</p>
      <a class="btn" href="/kindle-page-turner/">Read the page turner guide</a>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <span class="pill">Buying guide</span>
      <h2><a href="/kindle-case/">Kindle case buying guide</a></h2>
      <p>Why model year decides fit, the four main case styles compared, materials, features, and the red flags to look for in a listing.</p>
      <a class="btn" href="/kindle-case/">Read the case guide</a>
    </article>
  </div>

  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Sources first.</strong> Specs and prices come from Amazon's listings and announcements, backed by reputable press coverage, and each page lists them.</li>
    <li><strong>No invented numbers.</strong> If a spec is not published, we say so and send you to the Amazon listing.</li>
    <li><strong>Honest about testing.</strong> We do not claim to have tested products we have not handled.</li>
    <li><strong>Clear on money.</strong> We are an independent site, not Amazon or an authorized reseller. Read our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a> and <a href="/about/">editorial policy</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Start here</h2>
  <p>New to Kindle? Read the <a href="/kindle-paperwhite/#short">Paperwhite short answer</a>, then check <a href="/kindle-paperwhite-case/">Paperwhite case fit by model year</a> (or the <a href="/kindle-scribe-case/">Kindle Scribe case guide</a> if you write on your Kindle) and the general <a href="/kindle-case/#fit">case fit guide</a> before buying anything. Choosing between a flap and a shell? Read <a href="/kindle-cover/">Kindle covers explained</a>; for bags and bedside, see the <a href="/kindle-sleeve/">sleeve</a> and <a href="/kindle-stand/">stand</a> guides. Own a color Kindle? See the <a href="/kindle-colorsoft-case/">Colorsoft case guide</a>. Lost the cable or want hands-free reading? Start with the <a href="/kindle-charger/">charger</a> and <a href="/kindle-page-turner/">page turner</a> guides. Not sure where to begin? The <a href="/kindle-accessories/#matrix">accessories-by-model table</a> puts every guide in one place. Questions? See the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a>.</p>
</Base>
